hange using specified Cu(II)/Co(II) systems.","level":"a_level"},{"key":"28.2.6","parent":"28.2","topic":"28.2","title":"General characteristic chemical properties of the first set of transition elements, titanium to copper","description":"Use E° to assess transition-metal redox feasibility.","level":"a_level"},{"key":"28.2.7","parent":"28.2","topic":"28.2","title":"General characteristic chemical properties of the first set of transition elements, titanium to copper","description":"Describe/calculate specified permanganate/ethanedioate, permanganate/Fe²⁺ and Cu²⁺/I⁻ systems.","level":"a_level"},{"key":"28.2.8","parent":"28.2","topic":"28.2","title":"General characteristic chemical properties of the first set of transition elements, titanium to copper","description":"Perform other supplied redox calculations.","level":"a_level"},{"key":"28.3.1","parent":"28.3","topic":"28.3","title":"Colour of complexes","description":"Use degenerate/non-degenerate d-orbital terminology.","level":"a_level"},{"key":"28.3.2","parent":"28.3","topic":"28.3","title":"Colour of complexes","description":"Explain d-orbital splitting in octahedral/tetrahedral complexes.","level":"a_level"},{"key":"28.3.3","parent":"28.3","topic":"28.3","title":"Colour of complexes","description":"Explain colours via d-electron promotion and light absorption.","level":"a_level"},{"key":"28.3.4","parent":"28.3","topic":"28.3","title":"Colour of complexes","description":"Explain ligand effects on ΔE and complementary colour.","level":"a_level"},{"key":"28.3.5","parent":"28.3","topic":"28.3","title":"Colour of complexes","description":"Use Cu(II)/Co(II) ligand exchange to explain colour changes.","level":"a_level"},{"key":"28.4.1","parent":"28.4","topic":"28.4","title":"Stereoisomerism in transition element complexes","description":"Describe geometrical and optical stereoisomerism in complexes, including bidentate examples.","level":"a_level"},{"key":"28.4.2","parent":"28.4","topic":"28.4","title":"Stereoisomeri