 2","content":"Use energy cycles and relevant energy terms to calculate enthalpy changes that cannot be measured directly and to use bond-energy data.","topic":"5.2","objectives":["5.2.2"],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"5","outcomeIndex":2}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"topic","knowledge_key":"topic|6","title":"Electrochemistry","content":"Topic 6: Electrochemistry.","topic":"6","objectives":[],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"6"}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"topic","knowledge_key":"topic|6.1","title":"Redox processes: electron transfer and changes in oxidation number (oxidation state)","content":"6.1 Redox processes: electron transfer and changes in oxidation number (oxidation state)","topic":"6.1","objectives":[],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"6"}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"content_scope","knowledge_key":"scope|6.1","title":"Redox processes: electron transfer and changes in oxidation number (oxidation state)","content":"Electrochemistry: Redox processes: electron transfer and changes in oxidation number (oxidation state). This subsection is part of the AS Level Chemistry 9701 syllabus.","topic":"6.1","objectives":[],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"6"}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"learning_outcome","knowledge_key":"outcome|6.1|1","title":"Redox processes: electron transfer and changes in oxidation number (oxidation state): outcome 1","content":"Calculate oxidation numbers of elements in compounds and ions.","topic":"6.1","objectives":["6.1.1"],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"6","outcomeIndex":1}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"learning_outcome","knowledge_key":"outcome|6.1|2","title":"Redox processes: electron transfer and changes in oxidation number (oxidation state): outcome 2","content":"Use changes in oxidation numbers to help balance chemical equations.","topic":"6.1","objectives":["6.1.2"],"metadata":{"sourc