perties of the Group 17 elements: outcome 2","content":"Describe and explain the trend in bond strength of halogen molecules.","topic":"11.1","objectives":["11.1.2"],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11","outcomeIndex":2}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"learning_outcome","knowledge_key":"outcome|11.1|3","title":"Physical properties of the Group 17 elements: outcome 3","content":"Interpret volatility in terms of instantaneous dipole-induced dipole forces.","topic":"11.1","objectives":["11.1.3"],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11","outcomeIndex":3}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"topic","knowledge_key":"topic|11.2","title":"The chemical properties of the halogen elements and the hydrogen halides","content":"11.2 The chemical properties of the halogen elements and the hydrogen halides","topic":"11.2","objectives":[],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11"}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"content_scope","knowledge_key":"scope|11.2","title":"The chemical properties of the halogen elements and the hydrogen halides","content":"Group 17: The chemical properties of the halogen elements and the hydrogen halides. This subsection is part of the AS Level Chemistry 9701 syllabus.","topic":"11.2","objectives":[],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11"}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"learning_outcome","knowledge_key":"outcome|11.2|1","title":"The chemical properties of the halogen elements and the hydrogen halides: outcome 1","content":"Describe relative reactivity of halogen elements as oxidising agents.","topic":"11.2","objectives":["11.2.1"],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11","outcomeIndex":1}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"learning_outcome","knowledge_key":"outcome|11.2|2","title":"The chemical properties of the halogen elements and the hydrogen halides: outcome 2","content":"Describe reactions of halogen elements with hydrogen and explain their relative reactivity.","topic":"11.2","objectives":["11.2.2"],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11","outcomeIndex":2}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"learning_outcome","knowledge_key":"outcome|11.2|3","title":"The chemical properties of the halogen elements and the hydrogen halides: outcome 3","content":"Describe relative thermal stabilities of hydrogen halides and explain them using bond strengths.","topic":"11.2","objectives":["11.2.3"],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11","outcomeIndex":3}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"topic","knowledge_key":"topic|11.3","title":"Some reactions of the halide ions","content":"11.3 Some reactions of the halide ions","topic":"11.3","objectives":[],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11"}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"content_scope","knowledge_key":"scope|11.3","title":"Some reactions of the halide ions","content":"Group 17: Some reactions of the halide ions. This subsection is part of the AS Level Chemistry 9701 syllabus.","topic":"11.3","objectives":[],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11"}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"learning_outcome","knowledge_key":"outcome|11.3|1","title":"Some reactions of the halide ions: outcome 1","content":"Describe relative reactivity of halide ions as reducing agents.","topic":"11.3","objectives":["11.3.1"],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11","outcomeIndex":1}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"learning_outcome","knowledge_key":"outcome|11.3|2","title":"Some reactions of the halide ions: outcome 2","content":"Describe and explain halide-ion reactions with aqueous silver ions followed by aqueous ammonia and with concentrated sulfuric acid, including balanced equations.","topic":"11.3","objectives":["11.3.2"],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11","outcomeIndex":2}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"topic","knowledge_key":"topic|11.4","title":"The reactions of chlorine","content":"11.4 The reactions of chlorine","topic":"11.4","objectives":[],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11"}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"content_scope","knowledge_key":"scope|11.4","title":"The reactions of chlorine","content":"Group 17: The reactions of chlorine. This subsection is part of the AS Level Chemistry 9701 syllabus.","topic":"11.4","objectives":[],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11"}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"learning_outcome","knowledge_key":"outcome|11.4|1","title":"The reactions of chlorine: outcome 1","content":"Describe and interpret chlorine reactions with cold and hot aqueous sodium hydroxide in terms of oxidation-number changes and identify them as disproportionation.","topic":"11.4","objectives":["11.4.1"],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11","outcomeIndex":1}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"learning_outcome","knowledge_key":"outcome|11.4|2","title":"The reactions of chlorine: outcome 2","content":"Explain, including with an equation, the use of chlorine in water purification, including formation of HOCl and ClO- active species.","topic":"11.4","objectives":["11.4.2"],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"11","outcomeIndex":2}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"topic","knowledge_key":"topic|12","title":"Nitrogen and sulfur","content":"Topic 12: Nitrogen and sulfur.","topic":"12","objectives":[],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"12"}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"topic","knowledge_key":"topic|12.1","title":"Nitrogen and sulfur","content":"12.1 Nitrogen and sulfur","topic":"12.1","objectives":[],"metadata":{"source":"structured-cambridge-dataset","section":"12"}},{"level":"as_level","kind":"content_scope","knowledge_key":"scope|12.1","title":"Nitrogen and sulfur","content":"Nitrogen and sulfur: Nitrogen and sulfur. This subsection is part of the AS Level Chemistry 9701 syllabus.","topic":"1